    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31280" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nŏvēnus</span></b> , a, um,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>num. adj.
				distr.</i> [novem], <i>nine each, nine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut virgines ter novenae per urbem euntes carmen
					canerent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					27, 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terga novena boūm,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					12, 97</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">novenorum conceptu dierum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 5, 9, § 53</span></i>
			; in sing., <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 1,
				2, 4</span></i>.</div>
